WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.534 --> 00:00:04.170
-Our first guest tonight is
an Emmy-nominated comedian,

00:00:04.170 --> 00:00:05.839
producer, and actor you know
from his work

00:00:05.839 --> 00:00:07.740
in "Big Mouth",
"Oh, Hello on Broadway",

00:00:07.740 --> 00:00:09.041
and "Don't Worry Darling".

00:00:09.041 --> 00:00:11.844
His stand-up special,
"Nick Kroll: Little Big Boy"

00:00:11.844 --> 00:00:13.379
is now streaming globally
on Netflix.

00:00:13.379 --> 00:00:14.680
Let's take a look.

00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:16.115
-Part of the reason she wanted
to break up with me

00:00:16.115 --> 00:00:17.917
is she didn't, like, find me,
like, masculine enough.

00:00:17.917 --> 00:00:20.720
Like, she wanted a guy with,
like, sleeves of tattoos

00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:24.524
who could drive stick,
could ride a motorcycle.

00:00:24.524 --> 00:00:27.960
And I'm just never gonna be
the guy who rides a motorcycle.

00:00:27.960 --> 00:00:29.895
If I were, I'd be the guy
at the back of the pack

00:00:29.895 --> 00:00:33.833
who's like, "Oh, no, I'm gonna
miss the light.

00:00:33.833 --> 00:00:39.105
Aw, I'm gonna get split up
from the fellas.

00:00:39.105 --> 00:00:42.241
I was really looking forward to
rumbling through a neighborhood

00:00:42.241 --> 00:00:45.945
and ruining people's day."

00:00:45.945 --> 00:00:48.013
-Please welcome back to the show
our very good friend,

00:00:48.013 --> 00:00:49.415
Nick Kroll, everybody.

00:00:49.415 --> 00:00:51.584
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:51.584 --> 00:00:59.459 line:0%
♪♪

00:00:59.459 --> 00:01:07.366 line:0%
♪♪

00:01:07.366 --> 00:01:08.501
Hello, friend!

00:01:08.501 --> 00:01:09.968
-Hello!

00:01:09.968 --> 00:01:12.538
-This is a very -- These last
couple weeks have been

00:01:12.538 --> 00:01:13.539
very special for me.

00:01:13.539 --> 00:01:14.974
I haven't seen you in forever.

00:01:14.974 --> 00:01:16.976
And then I was lucky enough,
obviously, I'm seeing you now.

00:01:16.976 --> 00:01:19.012
You little boy is
1-and-a-half years old.

00:01:19.012 --> 00:01:20.280
-Yes.
-Congratulations.

00:01:20.280 --> 00:01:22.181
-Thank you very much.
-How is -- What's he into?

00:01:22.181 --> 00:01:24.584
-He's into S&amp;M.
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:24.584 --> 00:01:26.986
-It's so crazy.
-Yeah.

00:01:26.986 --> 00:01:28.454
-It's so weird I never --
-Well, yeah, and what're you

00:01:28.454 --> 00:01:29.956
gonna do, 'cause you gotta
support what --

00:01:29.956 --> 00:01:33.626
-You gotta support the kid.
-Yeah, you just let them choose

00:01:33.626 --> 00:01:35.428
their own path.
-He's on his journey.

00:01:35.428 --> 00:01:37.963
-Yeah. [ Laughs ]

00:01:37.963 --> 00:01:40.966
-He's also -- besides that, he's
really into high fives

00:01:40.966 --> 00:01:42.235
right now.
-Uh-huh.

00:01:42.235 --> 00:01:44.203
-High five, high five?
-Oh, he asks for it, yeah.

00:01:44.203 --> 00:01:45.471
-High five, high five?
-Yeah.

00:01:45.471 --> 00:01:47.540
-So, like, we'll be walking
the streets,

00:01:47.540 --> 00:01:50.443
and we're literally walking
through Brooklyn

00:01:50.443 --> 00:01:51.878
on Saturday,
and he's just going,

00:01:51.878 --> 00:01:53.212
"High five, high five?"

00:01:53.212 --> 00:01:55.681
And so, like, and he's
in my little BabyBjorn

00:01:55.681 --> 00:01:58.217
so I just have this tiny human
being like, "High five,

00:01:58.217 --> 00:01:59.585
high five?"
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:59.585 --> 00:02:03.055
-And it's so interesting to see
who will high five a baby

00:02:03.055 --> 00:02:04.056
and won't.
-Yeah.

00:02:04.056 --> 00:02:05.291
Is it who you think?

00:02:05.291 --> 00:02:07.093
Can you tell now when you see
someone coming,

00:02:07.093 --> 00:02:08.094
if they're gonna do it or not?

00:02:08.094 --> 00:02:09.195
-Kind of.
-Yeah.

00:02:09.195 --> 00:02:11.231
-Middle-aged white guys don't.
-Right.

00:02:12.865 --> 00:02:14.033
-Like --
-Well, that's the thing.

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:16.002
I mean, I say,
as a middle-aged white guy,

00:02:16.002 --> 00:02:18.104
you don't know what you're gonna
get canceled for.

00:02:18.104 --> 00:02:21.640
-[ Laughs ] These days.
-[ Laughs ]

00:02:21.640 --> 00:02:26.913
It used to be in the '80s
you could high five a baby.

00:02:26.913 --> 00:02:28.514
-Different time.

00:02:28.514 --> 00:02:32.384
The political correctness police
won't let you high five

00:02:32.384 --> 00:02:35.254
a random baby anymore.

00:02:35.254 --> 00:02:38.991
-[ Laughs ]
-But the truth is

00:02:38.991 --> 00:02:40.993
you will get canceled.

00:02:40.993 --> 00:02:42.361
-Yeah, I've been lucky enough
over the years

00:02:42.361 --> 00:02:43.496
to meet your parents.

00:02:43.496 --> 00:02:44.630
They're incredibly wonderful.

00:02:44.630 --> 00:02:46.565
I know they're wildly
supportive of you.

00:02:46.565 --> 00:02:48.468
-Yes.
-And yet, like, a lot

00:02:48.468 --> 00:02:51.004
of parents
of people who do stand-up sets,

00:02:51.004 --> 00:02:53.005
they get poked fun of a lot.

00:02:53.005 --> 00:02:55.107
You maybe have, and I'm not just
saying this,

00:02:55.107 --> 00:02:57.210
one of the best bits about moms
I've ever seen

00:02:57.210 --> 00:02:58.277
in a stand-up act.

00:02:58.277 --> 00:03:00.612
It is remarkably great.

00:03:00.612 --> 00:03:02.081
I've been quoting it ever since
I've seen it,

00:03:02.081 --> 00:03:03.349
but how did they react to it?

00:03:03.349 --> 00:03:06.185
-You know, it's like I talk --
I'll just, like --

00:03:06.185 --> 00:03:08.955
I'll set it up quickly in some
way, if that's --

00:03:08.955 --> 00:03:10.656
I'm lifting the curtain here,
folks.

00:03:10.656 --> 00:03:14.026
-[ Laughs ]
-So, you know, moms are --

00:03:14.026 --> 00:03:16.596
I have no shorter fuse
with anyone in my life

00:03:16.596 --> 00:03:17.730
than I do my own mother.
-Yeah.

00:03:17.730 --> 00:03:19.932
-You know, like, it doesn't
matter --

00:03:19.932 --> 00:03:22.969
My mom could be like,
"I clipped an article

00:03:22.969 --> 00:03:26.038
about the LA Art Deco movement."

00:03:26.038 --> 00:03:29.609
And I'm like, "Why would you do
that, Mom?"

00:03:31.611 --> 00:03:34.580
You know art deco's, like,
my least favorite architectural

00:03:34.580 --> 00:03:36.816
movement!"

00:03:36.816 --> 00:03:40.253
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:40.253 --> 00:03:43.155
-And then, dad's, like, get away
scot-free.

00:03:43.155 --> 00:03:44.890
It's like I remember my Dad
being like, "Hey, son,

00:03:44.890 --> 00:03:47.927
wanted to come to your baseball
game today, but then didn't."

00:03:47.927 --> 00:03:49.395
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:49.395 --> 00:03:52.398
-And I'm just like, "That's
okay, Daddy."

00:03:52.398 --> 00:03:53.532
-[ Laughs ]

00:03:53.532 --> 00:03:56.268
-So, the joke is --
there's a lot more.

00:03:56.268 --> 00:03:57.403
You should watch the special,

00:03:57.403 --> 00:04:00.473
and -- but, you know,
and it's so weird,

00:04:00.473 --> 00:04:02.307
because -- and I feel like it's
similar with your parents --

00:04:02.307 --> 00:04:04.677
it's like we are -- I don't know
if we're the exception,

00:04:04.677 --> 00:04:06.412
but we come from, like, very
loving, supportive...

00:04:06.412 --> 00:04:07.713
-We really do.
-...families.

00:04:07.713 --> 00:04:09.582
-And I think families who
thought there was something cool

00:04:09.582 --> 00:04:10.649
and noble about comedy.

00:04:10.649 --> 00:04:11.718
-Yes.
-Yeah.

00:04:11.718 --> 00:04:14.620
-And so my parents came
to my shows

00:04:14.620 --> 00:04:16.822
before I was doing anything.

00:04:16.822 --> 00:04:20.593
I was in the back of, like,
weird VHS, like, rental stores.

00:04:20.593 --> 00:04:22.662
-Yeah.
-It was porn.

00:04:22.662 --> 00:04:25.965
And so they would come
to those shows,

00:04:25.965 --> 00:04:27.266
and they would watch me bomb.

00:04:27.266 --> 00:04:28.667
They'd come to open mics.

00:04:28.667 --> 00:04:30.836
They'd come to bringer shows
where they would have to pay

00:04:30.836 --> 00:04:33.840
like $40 to see me and a bunch
of, like, 10 people

00:04:33.840 --> 00:04:35.575
who've never done comedy before.

00:04:35.575 --> 00:04:40.713
And, like, how do I repay them
to just, like very publicly

00:04:40.713 --> 00:04:45.785
make fun of them on a stand-up
special on Netflix,

00:04:45.785 --> 00:04:49.221
which you can't even get
on VHS anymore?

00:04:49.221 --> 00:04:50.489
-[ Laughs ] Yeah.

00:04:50.489 --> 00:04:52.391
-And so I want to take
this opportunity

00:04:52.391 --> 00:04:54.193
to look -- find my camera.
-There you go.

00:04:54.193 --> 00:04:55.394
-That's my camera.
-Yeah.

00:04:55.394 --> 00:04:58.297
-I want to say to my Mom
and my Dad,

00:04:58.297 --> 00:05:01.300
thank you very much for always
supporting me.

00:05:01.300 --> 00:05:06.705
I'm so sorry that I have made
fun of you in my stand-up,

00:05:06.705 --> 00:05:09.942
and also, frankly,
you deserve it.

00:05:09.942 --> 00:05:13.012
[ Laughter ]

00:05:13.012 --> 00:05:15.681
But I love you,
and I really am grateful.

00:05:15.681 --> 00:05:16.982
I'm grateful to my family.

00:05:16.982 --> 00:05:18.818
I'm grateful to my wife
for helping --

00:05:18.818 --> 00:05:21.353
-I actually want to ask
about your wife,

00:05:21.353 --> 00:05:23.122
because I've talked about mine
in stand-up, as well.

00:05:23.122 --> 00:05:24.724
We'll be right back with more
from Nick Kroll.

